var e={schemaVersion:1,apiVersion:`0.6.0-dev`,title:`UCSB XRP API reference`,introduction:`Open your project README.md first. It names the Python files and methods assigned to you. Use those class entries below for exact inputs, outputs, units, state, and required behavior. Other entries describe the supplied services and records those methods use.`,publicModules:{ucsb_xrp:`ArenaMap.DeliveryMission.DeliveryTask.DifferentialDriveBase.DriveCommand.GridCell.GridPath.GridPlannerBase.LineFollowerBase.NavigationConfig.NavigationControllerBase.RobotConfig.OccupancyGrid.OdometryBase.PoseCorrectorBase.RangeSafetyControllerBase.Rectangle.Measurements.MotionCommand.MotorEfforts.NavigationGoal.Pose.ProjectWorld.RawSensors.ReflectanceReadings.Robot.RobotState.SensorModelBase.STOP_COMMAND.StraightLineController.StraightTrialResult.VisitOrderPlannerBase.WheelSpeeds.WheelSpeedControllerBase.XRPBot.bearing_to_goal.clamp.distance_to_goal.elapsed_time_s.wrap_angle_rad.live.load_world.run_straight_trial`.split(`.`),"ucsb_xrp.live":[`LiveParameter`,`apply_updates`,`choice`,`number`,`plot`,`toggle`,`watch`]},conventions:[`Distances, positions, wheel travel, and range use millimeters (mm).`,`Linear and wheel speeds use millimeters per second (mm/s). Device timestamps use integer milliseconds; calculated elapsed time uses seconds.`,`Angles use radians and turn rates use radians per second. Positive heading and turn rate are counterclockwise.`,`A DriveCommand is dimensionless and each wheel command is within -1.0 to 1.0.`,`World +x is the reference forward direction and world +y points left. Positive wheel speed means forward wheel motion.`],sections:[{id:`components`,title:`Classes you implement`,introduction:`Complete the files named in your project README, keeping their class and method names. Each entry below specifies the input data, required calculation, and returned result. Test functions runs input/output examples against your files. For a class selected in course_setup.py, set its USE_STUDENT_* flag to True before Run; False selects the supplied implementation.`,entries:[{id:`sensor-model`,name:`SensorModel`,symbols:[`SensorModel`,`SensorModelBase`],kind:`project component`,projectFile:`sensor_model.py`,baseClass:`SensorModelBase`,configType:`RobotConfig`,purpose:`Calculates wheel travel, wheel-speed estimates, and the sampling interval from encoder counts and timestamps. Its update(raw) method receives a RawSensors record and returns a Measurements record; Robot.step() uses that result for feedback and odometry. The separate estimate_range() method, used in Out-and-Back, calculates a distance estimate from a set of ultrasound readings.`,state:`After reset(), retain the encoder and time zero values, the preceding sample, and enough recent encoder history to estimate wheel speed. Wheel position remains relative to the reset values.`,relevantConfigFields:[`sample_period_ms`,`wheel_diameter_mm`,`encoder_counts_per_revolution`,`left_encoder_sign`,`right_encoder_sign`,`wheel_speed_filter_time_constant_ms`],signature:`class SensorModel(SensorModelBase):`,parameters:[{name:`config`,type:`RobotConfig`,description:`Robot sampling, encoder, wheel, and wheel-speed-estimation settings. The same value is available inside the class as self.config.`}],exceptions:[`TypeError if config is not a RobotConfig value.`],methods:[{id:`method-sensor-model-reset`,name:`reset`,signature:`reset(raw: RawSensors) -> Measurements`,summary:`Establish the encoder and time origins for a new run.`,parameters:[{name:`raw`,type:`RawSensors`,description:`First hardware sample after Robot resets the encoders.`}],returns:{type:`Measurements`,description:`A measurement at raw.time_ms with zero positions, increments, speeds, and dt_s, while preserving raw.range_mm, raw.reflectance, and raw.button_pressed.`},exceptions:[`TypeError if raw is not a RawSensors value.`],requiredBehavior:[`Prepare update() to process the next chronological sample.`,`Reset all wheel-speed estimator history so the first reported speeds are zero.`]},{id:`method-sensor-model-update`,name:`update`,signature:`update(raw: RawSensors) -> Measurements`,summary:`Convert the next hardware sample into physical measurements.`,parameters:[{name:`raw`,type:`RawSensors`,description:`Next encoder, device-time, optional range and reflectance, and USER-button sample.`}],returns:{type:`Measurements`,description:`Cumulative wheel positions from the reset values, the latest unsmoothed wheel increments, wheel-speed estimates from recent encoder samples, elapsed time, optional range and reflectance, and button state.`},exceptions:[`RuntimeError if reset() has not been called.`,`TypeError if raw is not a RawSensors value.`],requiredBehavior:[`Apply the configured encoder signs, wheel diameter, and encoder counts per revolution.`,`Calculate dt_s from consecutive device timestamps with elapsed_time_s().`,`Do not smooth left_increment_mm or right_increment_mm; odometry uses the measured increments.`,`Estimate wheel speed from recent encoder samples or an equivalent estimator whose response is set by wheel_speed_filter_time_constant_ms. The exact estimator algorithm is not prescribed.`,`If no positive time has elapsed, report dt_s as zero without dividing by zero; positions and increments still follow the new encoder counts.`,`Preserve raw.range_mm, raw.reflectance, and raw.button_pressed in the returned Measurements.`]},{id:`method-sensor-model-estimate-range`,name:`estimate_range`,signature:`estimate_range(samples, minimum_usable: int) -> float | None`,summary:`Combine repeated ultrasonic readings while rejecting unusable values.`,parameters:[{name:`samples`,type:`sequence[float | None]`,units:`mm`,description:`Range readings to combine.`},{name:`minimum_usable`,type:`int`,description:`Minimum number of usable readings required; must be at least 1.`}],returns:{type:`float | None`,description:`Median of the finite, positive, non-Boolean readings, or None when too few usable readings remain.`},exceptions:[`TypeError if minimum_usable is not an integer or samples cannot be iterated.`,`ValueError if minimum_usable is less than 1.`]}],example:{title:`Example: measure travel between two encoder samples`,code:`from robot_config import ROBOT_CONFIG
from sensor_model import SensorModel
from ucsb_xrp import RawSensors

# RawSensors holds direct hardware readings; these two samples are test inputs.
model = SensorModel(ROBOT_CONFIG)  # Use after implementing SensorModel.
first = RawSensors(time_ms=0, left_encoder_count=0, right_encoder_count=0, range_mm=None, button_pressed=False)
model.reset(first)  # Establish the position and time origin.
# After 20 ms, the left count is 4 and the right count is 5.
second = RawSensors(time_ms=20, left_encoder_count=4, right_encoder_count=5, range_mm=None, button_pressed=False)
measurement = model.update(second)
print(measurement.left_increment_mm)  # Travel since the first sample, in mm.
print(measurement.left_speed_mm_s)  # Speed estimate, in mm/s.`},constructorSignature:`SensorModel(config: RobotConfig)`},{id:`wheel-speed-controller`,name:`WheelSpeedController`,symbols:[`WheelSpeedController`,`WheelSpeedControllerBase`],kind:`project component`,projectFile:`wheel_speed_controller.py`,baseClass:`WheelSpeedControllerBase`,configType:`RobotConfig`,purpose:`Calculates the motor command needed for each wheel from its requested speed and measured speed. Its update(target, measured) method receives two WheelSpeeds records and returns a DriveCommand. Robot.step() calls this method and sends the returned commands to the motors.`,state:`The controller may retain values needed from earlier samples. reset() must return all retained controller values to their initial condition.`,relevantConfigFields:[`left_start_command`,`right_start_command`,`left_speed_command_gain`,`right_speed_command_gain`,`wheel_speed_kp`,`max_drive_command`],signature:`class WheelSpeedController(WheelSpeedControllerBase):`,parameters:[{name:`config`,type:`RobotConfig`,description:`Motor calibration, feedback gain, and command limit. The same value is available inside the class as self.config.`}],exceptions:[`TypeError if config is not a RobotConfig value.`],methods:[{id:`method-wheel-speed-controller-reset`,name:`reset`,signature:`reset() -> None`,summary:`Prepare controller state for a new run.`,returns:{type:`None`,description:`No value.`}},{id:`method-wheel-speed-controller-update`,name:`update`,signature:`update(target: WheelSpeeds, measured: WheelSpeeds) -> DriveCommand`,summary:`Calculate the next motor command for both wheels.`,parameters:[{name:`target`,type:`WheelSpeeds`,units:`mm/s`,description:`Requested left and right wheel speeds from DifferentialDrive.`},{name:`measured`,type:`WheelSpeeds`,units:`mm/s`,description:`Latest wheel-speed estimates formed from recent encoder samples by SensorModel.`}],returns:{type:`DriveCommand`,description:`Normalized left and right motor commands whose magnitudes do not exceed config.max_drive_command.`},exceptions:[`TypeError if target or measured is not a WheelSpeeds value.`],requiredBehavior:[`Return an exact zero command for a wheel whose requested speed is zero.`,`Keep each command within plus or minus config.max_drive_command.`,`For a nonzero requested speed, increasing the speed error in the requested direction must not weaken the command. Before the command reaches config.max_drive_command, the larger speed error must produce a stronger command under the same conditions.`]}],constructorSignature:`WheelSpeedController(config: RobotConfig)`},{id:`differential-drive`,name:`DifferentialDrive`,symbols:[`DifferentialDrive`,`DifferentialDriveBase`],kind:`project component`,projectFile:`differential_drive.py`,baseClass:`DifferentialDriveBase`,configType:`RobotConfig`,purpose:`Calculates left and right wheel speeds from the requested forward speed, turn rate, and distance between the wheels. Its wheel_speeds(command) method reads a MotionCommand and returns a WheelSpeeds record. Robot.step() passes those wheel speeds to the wheel-speed controller.`,state:`None. Each wheel_speeds() calculation depends only on its MotionCommand and the configured track width.`,relevantConfigFields:[`track_width_mm`],signature:`class DifferentialDrive(DifferentialDriveBase):`,parameters:[{name:`config`,type:`RobotConfig`,description:`Robot geometry containing the effective track width. The same value is available inside the class as self.config.`}],exceptions:[`TypeError if config is not a RobotConfig value.`],methods:[{id:`method-differential-drive-wheel-speeds`,name:`wheel_speeds`,signature:`wheel_speeds(command: MotionCommand) -> WheelSpeeds`,summary:`Calculate target wheel speeds for one body-motion request.`,parameters:[{name:`command`,type:`MotionCommand`,description:`Requested forward speed and counterclockwise turn rate.`}],returns:{type:`WheelSpeeds`,description:`Target left and right wheel speeds in mm/s.`},exceptions:[`TypeError if command is not a MotionCommand value.`],requiredBehavior:[`Produce wheel speeds consistent with planar differential-drive kinematics and config.track_width_mm.`,`Zero turn rate produces equal wheel speeds. Positive turn rate produces a greater right-wheel speed than left-wheel speed; negative turn rate reverses that relationship.`,`Support straight motion, in-place rotation, and simultaneous forward motion and turning.`]}],constructorSignature:`DifferentialDrive(config: RobotConfig)`},{id:`odometry`,name:`Odometry`,symbols:[`Odometry`,`OdometryBase`],kind:`project component`,projectFile:`odometry.py`,baseClass:`OdometryBase`,configType:`RobotConfig`,purpose:`Estimates robot position and heading by accumulating the movement calculated from each pair of wheel-travel increments. Robot.step() supplies those increments to this class's update() method, which returns the updated Pose. reset(initial_pose) sets the position and heading at the start of a run.`,state:`After reset(), retain the latest Pose. The estimate uses measured wheel travel only; simulator ground truth is not an input.`,relevantConfigFields:[`track_width_mm`],signature:`class Odometry(OdometryBase):`,parameters:[{name:`config`,type:`RobotConfig`,description:`Robot geometry containing the effective track width. The same value is available inside the class as self.config.`}],exceptions:[`TypeError if config is not a RobotConfig value.`],properties:[{name:`pose`,type:`Pose`,description:`Latest estimated pose; available after reset().`}],methods:[{id:`method-odometry-reset`,name:`reset`,signature:`reset(initial_pose: Pose) -> Pose`,summary:`Set the pose for a new run.`,parameters:[{name:`initial_pose`,type:`Pose`,description:`Known starting position and heading.`}],returns:{type:`Pose`,description:`The established initial pose.`},exceptions:[`TypeError if initial_pose is not a Pose value.`]},{id:`method-odometry-update`,name:`update`,signature:`update(left_increment_mm: float, right_increment_mm: float) -> Pose`,summary:`Integrate one differential-drive wheel-travel increment.`,parameters:[{name:`left_increment_mm`,type:`float`,units:`mm`,description:`Signed left-wheel travel since the preceding sample.`},{name:`right_increment_mm`,type:`float`,units:`mm`,description:`Signed right-wheel travel since the preceding sample.`}],returns:{type:`Pose`,description:`Updated pose with heading wrapped to [-pi, pi).`},exceptions:[`RuntimeError if reset() has not been called.`,`TypeError for Boolean or nonnumeric increments.`],requiredBehavior:[`Equal wheel increments translate the pose without changing its heading. Equal and opposite increments rotate the pose about the midpoint between the wheels.`,`Unequal increments follow the exact constant-curvature arc implied by the two wheel paths; do not replace a finite turn with a straight-line approximation.`,`Wrap the updated heading to [-pi, pi), retain the new Pose, and return it.`]}],constructorSignature:`Odometry(config: RobotConfig)`},{id:`navigation-controller`,name:`NavigationController`,symbols:[`NavigationController`,`NavigationControllerBase`],kind:`project component`,projectFile:`navigation_controller.py`,baseClass:`NavigationControllerBase`,configType:`NavigationConfig`,purpose:`Chooses forward speed and turn rate to reach a sequence of positions and, where specified, headings. start(goals) stores the ordered route; update(pose) compares the current Pose with the active goal and returns a MotionCommand. The main program passes that command to Robot.step() and repeats until the route is complete.`,state:`Retain the ordered goals, the active goal, completion state, and any turning, driving, or final-alignment state used by the implementation.`,signature:`class NavigationController(NavigationControllerBase):`,parameters:[{name:`config`,type:`NavigationConfig`,description:`Travel speeds, turn rate, slowdown distance, and position and heading tolerances. The same value is available inside the class as self.config.`}],exceptions:[`TypeError if config is not a NavigationConfig value.`],methods:[{id:`method-navigation-controller-set-config`,name:`set_config`,signature:`set_config(config: NavigationConfig) -> None`,summary:`Replace navigation settings without resetting the active goal or controller mode. Inherited from NavigationControllerBase; course programs apply changed live speed and turn controls after a robot sample.`,parameters:[{name:`config`,type:`NavigationConfig`,description:`The complete replacement navigation settings.`}],returns:{type:`None`,description:`No value; the active route and mode remain intact.`},exceptions:[`TypeError if config is not a NavigationConfig value.`]},{id:`method-navigation-controller-start`,name:`start`,signature:`start(goals: sequence[NavigationGoal]) -> None`,summary:`Store an ordered goal sequence and begin navigation.`,parameters:[{name:`goals`,type:`sequence[NavigationGoal]`,description:`Tuple or list of navigation goals in visit order; it may be empty.`}],returns:{type:`None`,description:`No value.`},requiredBehavior:[`An empty goal sequence is immediately complete; current_goal() returns None and update() returns STOP_COMMAND.`],exceptions:[`TypeError if goals is not a tuple or list or contains a value other than NavigationGoal.`]},{id:`method-navigation-controller-update`,name:`update`,signature:`update(pose: Pose) -> MotionCommand`,summary:`Calculate the next motion request from the latest odometry pose.`,parameters:[{name:`pose`,type:`Pose`,description:`Current odometry estimate.`}],returns:{type:`MotionCommand`,description:`Forward-speed and turn-rate request for the next Robot step.`},requiredBehavior:[`Use wrap-safe heading errors.`,`Turn toward a goal before driving forward when the heading error is large.`,`Use approach speed within config.slowdown_distance_mm of the goal and realign if the heading error grows beyond config.realign_heading_rad.`,`Visit goals in their supplied order. A goal with heading_rad=None requires position only; a numerical final heading must also be reached.`,`After all goals are complete, return STOP_COMMAND.`],exceptions:[`TypeError if pose is not a Pose value.`]},{id:`method-navigation-controller-current-goal`,name:`current_goal`,signature:`current_goal() -> NavigationGoal | None`,summary:`Return the active goal, or None after completion.`,returns:{type:`NavigationGoal | None`,description:`Current goal or None.`}},{id:`method-navigation-controller-is-complete`,name:`is_complete`,signature:`is_complete() -> bool`,summary:`Report whether every required position and heading is complete.`,returns:{type:`bool`,description:`True only after the complete goal sequence has been reached.`}}],constructorSignature:`NavigationController(config: NavigationConfig)`},{id:`grid-planner`,name:`GridPlanner`,symbols:[`GridPlanner`,`GridPlannerBase`],kind:`project component`,projectFile:`grid_planner.py`,baseClass:`GridPlannerBase`,purpose:`Finds a route from a start cell to a goal cell without entering blocked cells. plan(grid, start, goal) receives an OccupancyGrid and two GridCell values, then returns the ordered cells in a GridPath, or None when no route exists. The main program converts those cells to positions for navigation.`,state:`None is required between calls. Search data may remain local to one plan() calculation.`,signature:`class GridPlanner(GridPlannerBase):`,methods:[{id:`method-grid-planner-plan`,name:`plan`,signature:`plan(grid: OccupancyGrid, start: GridCell | None, goal: GridCell | None) -> GridPath | None`,summary:`Find a valid connected route from the start cell to the goal cell.`,parameters:[{name:`grid`,type:`OccupancyGrid`,description:`Map of free and blocked cells.`},{name:`start`,type:`GridCell | None`,description:`Starting cell, or None when the position lies outside the grid.`},{name:`goal`,type:`GridCell | None`,description:`Destination cell, or None when the position lies outside the grid.`}],returns:{type:`GridPath | None`,description:`A route including both endpoints, or None when an endpoint is unavailable or blocked or no route exists.`},requiredBehavior:[`Use only free cells and move between cells that share a horizontal or vertical edge.`,`Any route that connects the endpoints through free edge-adjacent cells is accepted.`],exceptions:[`TypeError if grid is not OccupancyGrid or a non-None endpoint is not GridCell.`]}],example:{title:`Example: construct a grid for a software check`,code:`from course_setup import make_grid_planner
from ucsb_xrp import GridCell, OccupancyGrid

# Row-major cells: the middle cell of the lower row is blocked.
grid = OccupancyGrid(100.0, 0.0, 0.0, 3, 2, [False, True, False, False, False, False])
start = GridCell(0, 0)
goal = GridCell(2, 0)
path = make_grid_planner().plan(grid, start, goal)
print("No route" if path is None else path.cells)`},notes:[`The example constructs a small row-major grid solely for a software test. In a course project, construct the grid from an ArenaMap with OccupancyGrid.from_arena().`],constructorSignature:`GridPlanner()`}]},{id:`challenge-extension-components`,title:`Other classes assigned in specific challenges`,introduction:`Arena Line Circuit assigns LineFollower. Later extension projects may assign RangeSafetyController, PoseCorrector, or VisitOrderPlanner. Your project README.md identifies the methods to complete.`,entries:[{id:`line-follower`,name:`LineFollower`,symbols:[`LineFollower`,`LineFollowerBase`],kind:`project component`,projectFile:`line_follower.py`,baseClass:`LineFollowerBase`,purpose:`Calculates forward speed and turn rate from the left and right floor-sensor readings. Its update(reflectance, dt_s) method returns a MotionCommand that the main program passes to Robot.step() to follow the tape line.`,state:`After reset(), retain the preceding line error and any integral or derivative state used by the chosen feedback law. line_error exposes the latest left-minus-right reading difference.`,signature:`class LineFollower(LineFollowerBase):`,parameters:[{name:`settings`,type:`dict`,description:`Settings from robot_config.py, stored by the base class as self.settings. cruise_speed_mm_s and maximum_turn_rate_rad_s bound the output. minimum_speed_mm_s and turn_slowdown support speed reduction in turns. kp_rad_s, ki_rad_s2, kd_rad, and integral_limit_s support P, PI, PD, or PID designs when used.`}],methods:[{id:`method-line-follower-reset`,name:`reset`,signature:`reset() -> None`,summary:`Clear retained feedback state before a run.`,requiredBehavior:[`Set line_error and retained integral and preceding-error state to zero.`],returns:{type:`None`,description:`No value.`}},{id:`method-line-follower-update`,name:`update`,signature:`update(reflectance: ReflectanceReadings, dt_s: float) -> MotionCommand`,summary:`Return the next local motion request from one reflectance sample.`,parameters:[{name:`reflectance`,type:`ReflectanceReadings`,description:`Normalized left and right readings: 0 is a light floor and 1 is a dark line.`},{name:`dt_s`,type:`float`,units:`s`,description:`Elapsed sample interval used by derivative or integral terms.`}],returns:{type:`MotionCommand`,description:`Forward speed and turn rate for the next Robot.step() call.`},requiredBehavior:[`Use positive left-minus-right line error for a positive counterclockwise turn request.`,`Keep forward speed between zero and settings["cruise_speed_mm_s"], and absolute turn rate no greater than settings["maximum_turn_rate_rad_s"]. Choose the feedback law; proportional, derivative, and integral terms are available but not all required.`,`Do not use a stored world-coordinate route; this component is local reflectance feedback.`]}],notes:[`LineFollowerBase is imported from ucsb_xrp and supplies settings plus resettable feedback state.`],constructorSignature:`LineFollower(settings: dict)`},{id:`range-safety-controller`,name:`RangeSafetyController`,symbols:[`RangeSafetyController`,`RangeSafetyControllerBase`],kind:`project component`,projectFile:`range_safety_controller.py`,baseClass:`RangeSafetyControllerBase`,purpose:`Calculates how much of a requested forward speed to allow, using the current forward speed and distance to an obstacle. Its result is a nonnegative speed request; the program uses zero to request a stop.`,state:`Retain the configured response time, minimum deceleration, stopping margin, and maximum speed.`,signature:`class RangeSafetyController(RangeSafetyControllerBase):`,methods:[{id:`method-range-safety-controller-update`,name:`update`,signature:`update(requested_speed_mm_s: float, measured_speed_mm_s: float, range_mm: float | None) -> float`,summary:`Return a forward-speed request that preserves the configured stopping margin.`,parameters:[{name:`requested_speed_mm_s`,type:`float`,units:`mm/s`,description:`Nominal requested forward speed.`},{name:`measured_speed_mm_s`,type:`float`,units:`mm/s`,description:`Latest measured forward speed.`},{name:`range_mm`,type:`float | None`,units:`mm`,description:`Filtered forward range, or None when unavailable.`}],returns:{type:`float`,description:`A nonnegative request no greater than the nominal request or configured maximum.`},requiredBehavior:[`Return zero when range is unavailable or the configured stopping margin cannot be preserved.`,`Include the configured response interval and minimum deceleration when deciding whether continued motion is admissible.`,`Do not command reverse motion as part of this component.`]}],notes:[`The project class inherits RangeSafetyControllerBase, which validates and stores the four constructor settings.`],parameters:[{name:`response_time_s`,type:`float`,units:`s`,description:`Nonnegative time allowed for sensing and control response before braking.`},{name:`minimum_deceleration_mm_s2`,type:`float`,units:`mm/s²`,description:`Positive minimum braking deceleration assumed by the speed limit.`},{name:`stop_margin_mm`,type:`float`,units:`mm`,description:`Nonnegative distance to leave between the robot and an obstacle after stopping.`},{name:`maximum_speed_mm_s`,type:`float`,units:`mm/s`,description:`Positive upper bound for a forward-speed request.`}],constructorSignature:`RangeSafetyController(response_time_s, minimum_deceleration_mm_s2, stop_margin_mm, maximum_speed_mm_s)`},{id:`pose-corrector`,name:`PoseCorrector`,symbols:[`PoseCorrector`,`PoseCorrectorBase`],kind:`project component`,projectFile:`pose_corrector.py`,baseClass:`PoseCorrectorBase`,purpose:`Corrects estimated x or y position using a range measurement toward a known wall. The class stores the resulting position offset and applies it to later odometry positions. It leaves the odometry heading unchanged.`,state:`After reset(), retain independent x and y translation corrections.`,signature:`class PoseCorrector(PoseCorrectorBase):`,methods:[{id:`method-pose-corrector-reset`,name:`reset`,signature:`reset(raw_pose: Pose) -> Pose`,summary:`Clear prior translation corrections and establish the initial corrected pose.`,parameters:[{name:`raw_pose`,type:`Pose`,description:`Current uncorrected odometry pose.`}],returns:{type:`Pose`,description:`Initial corrected pose with the raw heading preserved.`}},{id:`method-pose-corrector-observe-x`,name:`observe_x`,signature:`observe_x(raw_pose: Pose, range_mm: float, wall_x_mm: float, facing_positive_x: bool) -> Pose`,summary:`Use a known x-normal wall observation to update only the x correction.`,returns:{type:`Pose`,description:`Corrected pose with the inferred x coordinate.`},requiredBehavior:[`Infer x from the known wall coordinate, sensor offset, range, and facing direction without changing the retained y correction.`]},{id:`method-pose-corrector-observe-y`,name:`observe_y`,signature:`observe_y(raw_pose: Pose, range_mm: float, wall_y_mm: float, facing_positive_y: bool) -> Pose`,summary:`Use a known y-normal wall observation to update only the y correction.`,returns:{type:`Pose`,description:`Corrected pose with the inferred y coordinate.`},requiredBehavior:[`Infer y from the known wall coordinate, sensor offset, range, and facing direction without changing the retained x correction.`]},{id:`method-pose-corrector-corrected-pose`,name:`corrected_pose`,signature:`corrected_pose(raw_pose: Pose) -> Pose`,summary:`Apply the retained translation to a raw odometry pose.`,parameters:[{name:`raw_pose`,type:`Pose`,description:`Current uncorrected odometry pose.`}],returns:{type:`Pose`,description:`Translated pose with raw_pose.heading_rad unchanged.`},requiredBehavior:[`reset() must have been called before this method.`]}],notes:[`The project class inherits PoseCorrectorBase, which validates and stores sensor_forward_offset_mm.`],parameters:[{name:`sensor_forward_offset_mm`,type:`float`,units:`mm`,description:`Nonnegative forward distance from the robot pose origin to the range sensor.`}],constructorSignature:`PoseCorrector(sensor_forward_offset_mm)`},{id:`visit-order-planner`,name:`VisitOrderPlanner`,symbols:[`VisitOrderPlanner`,`VisitOrderPlannerBase`],kind:`project component`,projectFile:`visit_order_planner.py`,baseClass:`VisitOrderPlannerBase`,purpose:`Finds the least-cost order for visiting specified stops. Its plan() method uses the cost of travel between each pair of stops, the start, required stops, and finish; it returns their visit order, or None when no complete route exists.`,state:`None is required between calls.`,signature:`class VisitOrderPlanner(VisitOrderPlannerBase):`,methods:[{id:`method-visit-order-planner-plan`,name:`plan`,signature:`plan(cost_table, start_index: int, required_indices: sequence[int], finish_index: int) -> tuple[int, ...] | None`,summary:`Return the least-cost complete visit order.`,parameters:[{name:`cost_table`,type:`sequence[sequence[float | None]]`,description:`Square pairwise route-cost table; None marks an unavailable directed connection.`},{name:`start_index`,type:`int`,description:`First node in the returned order.`},{name:`required_indices`,type:`sequence[int]`,description:`Distinct stops to visit exactly once.`},{name:`finish_index`,type:`int`,description:`Final node; it may equal start_index.`}],returns:{type:`tuple[int, ...] | None`,description:`Start, every required stop exactly once, and finish in least-cost order, or None when no complete order is reachable.`},requiredBehavior:[`Sum only available pairwise costs along a candidate order.`,`Break equal-cost ties by lexicographic tuple order.`,`Reject duplicate required stops and indices outside the table.`]}],notes:[`The project class inherits VisitOrderPlannerBase.`],constructorSignature:`VisitOrderPlanner()`}]},{id:`robot-services`,title:`Robot services`,introduction:`Use Robot for ordinary course programs. It assembles the selected components and performs the timed sequence of motor commands, sensor readings, measurements, and odometry in each Robot.step() call.`,entries:[{id:`robot`,name:`Robot`,symbols:[`Robot`],kind:`supplied class`,import:`from ucsb_xrp import Robot`,purpose:`Coordinates sensing and motor control. Each step(command) call calculates wheel-speed targets, updates motor commands, waits for the next sample, reads the sensors, updates position, and records telemetry. It returns a RobotState containing the new measurements and estimated Pose. Course projects create this object with make_robot(ROBOT_CONFIG).`,state:`After start(), retain the selected classes, latest RobotState, next absolute sample time, and latest timing overrun.`,signature:`Robot(config, bot, sensor_model, wheel_controller, differential_drive, odometry)`,parameters:[{name:`config`,type:`RobotConfig`,description:`Timing, geometry, calibration, gains, and limits.`},{name:`bot`,type:`XRPBot`,description:`Constructed physical or simulated hardware boundary.`},{name:`sensor_model`,type:`SensorModel`,description:`Constructed selected sensor interpretation component.`},{name:`wheel_controller`,type:`WheelSpeedController`,description:`Constructed selected wheel-speed controller.`},{name:`differential_drive`,type:`DifferentialDrive`,description:`Constructed selected body-to-wheel conversion component.`},{name:`odometry`,type:`Odometry`,description:`Constructed selected pose-estimation component.`}],exceptions:[`TypeError if config is not RobotConfig or a supplied object does not provide the methods required by Robot.`],properties:[{name:`config`,type:`RobotConfig`,description:`Robot configuration supplied at construction.`},{name:`state`,type:`RobotState`,description:`Latest state; raises RuntimeError before start().`},{name:`last_overrun_ms`,type:`int`,units:`ms`,description:`Amount by which the latest calculation exceeded its sample deadline, or zero.`},{name:`range_sample_seq`,type:`int | None`,description:`Identity of the latest requested ultrasound attempt in this run. Missing echoes have identities too. Repeated requests during the 70 ms minimum acquisition interval retain the same identity; None means no attempt is available in this run.`},{name:`range_sample_age_s`,type:`float | None`,units:`s`,description:`Elapsed time since that attempt completed, including an attempt with no usable echo. None before the first available attempt.`}],methods:[{id:`method-robot-start`,name:`start`,signature:`start(initial_pose: Pose, read_reflectance: bool = False) -> RobotState`,summary:`Reset encoders and components and begin a run.`,parameters:[{name:`initial_pose`,type:`Pose`,description:`Known starting pose.`},{name:`read_reflectance`,type:`bool`,default:`False`,description:`Include left/right floor reflectance in the initial sample.`}],returns:{type:`RobotState`,description:`Initial zero-travel measurement and pose.`},requiredBehavior:[`An IDE-managed Run begins immediately. A project launched directly on the XRP waits for the USER button.`],exceptions:[`TypeError if initial_pose is not a Pose value or read_reflectance is not Boolean.`,`Hardware or component exceptions raised while resetting or taking the initial sample.`]},{id:`method-robot-step`,name:`step`,signature:`step(command: MotionCommand, read_range: bool = False, read_reflectance: bool = False) -> RobotState`,summary:`Execute one complete robot control cycle.`,parameters:[{name:`command`,type:`MotionCommand`,description:`Requested body motion.`},{name:`read_range`,type:`bool`,default:`False`,description:`Request forward range; returns the most recent outcome during the 70 ms ultrasound interval. Check range_sample_seq and range_sample_age_s when freshness matters.`},{name:`read_reflectance`,type:`bool`,default:`False`,description:`Request left/right floor reflectance for this sample.`}],returns:{type:`RobotState`,description:`New measurements and odometry pose.`},requiredBehavior:[`Stops the motors before re-raising an exception from the cycle.`,`Uses the configured absolute sample schedule and skips missed deadlines; actual intervals can be longer because of hardware reads or program work; do not add sleep_ms() inside the control loop.`],exceptions:[`RuntimeError if start() has not been called.`,`TypeError if command is not MotionCommand or either read flag is not Boolean.`,`Hardware or component exceptions raised during the sample; Robot attempts to stop the motors before re-raising them.`]},{id:`robot-collect-range-samples`,name:`collect_range_samples`,signature:`collect_range_samples(count: int, timeout_s: float = 2.0) -> list[float | None]`,summary:`Collect distinct stationary ultrasound attempts while continuing stopped control steps.`,parameters:[{name:`count`,type:`int`,description:`Positive number of new attempts to collect. Equal numeric distances count separately; held readings do not.`},{name:`timeout_s`,type:`float`,units:`s`,default:`2.0`,description:`Positive elapsed collection limit. Increase explicitly for larger counts or slow control periods; the deadline is checked between sensor reads.`}],returns:{type:`list[float | None]`,description:`One entry per new attempt, including None for each missing echo. robot.state remains the latest state.`},requiredBehavior:[`Call start() first and confirm from measured wheel speeds that the robot has stopped. Every collection step requests STOP_COMMAND.`,`Counts distinct attempts, not statistically independent measurements. A stream of missing echoes completes normally.`,`Stops the motors before propagating a collection failure.`],exceptions:[`TypeError or ValueError for invalid count or timeout_s.`,`RuntimeError before start(), or when the elapsed collection limit expires before enough new attempts arrive.`,`Hardware or component exceptions raised during a control step.`]},{id:`method-robot-estimate-range`,name:`estimate_range`,signature:`estimate_range(samples, minimum_usable: int) -> float | None`,summary:`Use the selected SensorModel to combine range readings.`,parameters:[{name:`samples`,type:`sequence[float | None]`,units:`mm`,description:`Range readings to combine.`},{name:`minimum_usable`,type:`int`,description:`Minimum number of usable readings required.`}],returns:{type:`float | None`,description:`Range estimate in mm, or None.`},exceptions:[`TypeError if samples cannot be iterated, an element is not a number or None, or minimum_usable is not an integer. This catches program values such as a string before they can be mistaken for a missing sensor reading.`,`ValueError if minimum_usable is less than 1.`,`Exceptions raised by the selected SensorModel after input validation.`]},{id:`method-robot-stop`,name:`stop`,signature:`stop() -> None`,summary:`Stop both motors and publish a zero drive command.`,returns:{type:`None`,description:`No value.`},exceptions:[`Hardware exception if the motors cannot be stopped.`]}],example:{title:`Example: run the selected robot components`,code:`from course_setup import make_robot
from robot_config import ROBOT_CONFIG
from ucsb_xrp import MotionCommand, load_world

robot = make_robot(ROBOT_CONFIG)
try:  # Run the steps that need motor cleanup.
    state = robot.start(load_world().initial_pose)
    state = robot.step(MotionCommand(0.0, 0.0))
    print(state.pose.x_mm)
finally:  # Stop after normal completion or a Python error.
    robot.stop()`},notes:[`Course projects normally call make_robot(ROBOT_CONFIG) from course_setup.py. The manual Robot constructor is for advanced assembly and software tests.`,`In manual assembly, bot, sensor_model, wheel_controller, differential_drive, and odometry are constructed instances, not class names or configuration values.`]},{id:`run-straight-trial`,name:`run_straight_trial`,symbols:[`run_straight_trial`,`StraightTrialResult`],kind:`supplied function`,import:`from ucsb_xrp import run_straight_trial`,purpose:`Run a straight-distance experiment using your function to choose forward speed from the measured distance remaining. The supplied loop records data and stops the motors on completion, Stop, or an exception.`,signature:`run_straight_trial(robot, initial_pose, target_distance_mm, speed_for_distance)`,parameters:[{name:`robot`,type:`Robot`,description:`Robot assembled with the selected sensing and control classes.`},{name:`initial_pose`,type:`Pose`,description:`Starting position and heading from world.json.`},{name:`target_distance_mm`,type:`float`,units:`mm`,description:`Positive forward travel to the target.`},{name:`speed_for_distance`,type:`callable`,description:`Your function receives remaining distance in mm and returns forward speed from 0 to 240 mm/s. Returning zero requests the final stop; the function is no longer called during that run.`}],returns:{type:`StraightTrialResult`,description:`reason, final state (RobotState), remaining_mm, and motion_time_s. Positive remaining_mm means short of the target; negative means overshoot, based on average wheel travel.`},notes:[`Declare live.number controls once in your stopping_controller.py file and read their .value inside the function to use slider changes.`,`The loop publishes remaining_mm, requested_speed_mm_s, and motion_time_s. Motion time is estimated from wheel-speed samples above 5 mm/s, ending at the first rest sample in the final 0.3 s confirmation. It excludes confirmation time; it is not an independent floor measurement.`,`A normal stop reports stationary; a zero request before detected movement reports no_motion. The loop stops an unfinished run after 30 s or travel exceeding 1.5 times the target, reporting timeout or travel_limit.`,`The caller supplies the stopping rule. No distance-control implementation is selected automatically.`],example:{title:`Example: run your straight-distance experiment`,code:`from challenge import INITIAL_POSE, TRAVEL_DISTANCE_MM
from course_setup import make_robot
from robot_config import ROBOT_CONFIG
from stopping_controller import speed_for_distance
from ucsb_xrp import run_straight_trial

run_straight_trial(make_robot(ROBOT_CONFIG), INITIAL_POSE, TRAVEL_DISTANCE_MM, speed_for_distance)`}},{id:`straight-line-controller`,name:`StraightLineController`,symbols:[`StraightLineController`],kind:`supplied class`,import:`from ucsb_xrp import StraightLineController`,purpose:`Generate a straight-ahead MotionCommand from measured mean wheel travel, using cruise speed far from the target, approach speed near it, and zero speed at completion.`,state:`After start(), retain the initial mean wheel position, requested travel distance, and completion state.`,signature:`StraightLineController(config: NavigationConfig)`,parameters:[{name:`config`,type:`NavigationConfig`,description:`Cruise and approach speeds, slowdown distance, and position tolerance.`}],exceptions:[`TypeError if config is not a NavigationConfig value.`],methods:[{id:`method-straight-line-controller-start`,name:`start`,signature:`start(measurements: Measurements, distance_mm: float) -> None`,summary:`Begin a nonnegative forward move from the current mean wheel position.`,parameters:[{name:`measurements`,type:`Measurements`,description:`Measurements at the beginning of the move.`},{name:`distance_mm`,type:`float`,units:`mm`,description:`Requested nonnegative forward travel.`}],returns:{type:`None`,description:`No value.`},exceptions:[`TypeError if measurements is not a Measurements value.`,`ValueError if distance_mm is Boolean, nonnumeric, nonfinite, or negative.`]},{id:`method-straight-line-controller-update`,name:`update`,signature:`update(measurements: Measurements) -> MotionCommand`,summary:`Return cruise, approach, or stop command from remaining distance.`,parameters:[{name:`measurements`,type:`Measurements`,description:`Latest measured wheel positions.`}],returns:{type:`MotionCommand`,description:`Next straight-line motion request.`},exceptions:[`RuntimeError if start() has not been called.`,`TypeError if measurements is not a Measurements value.`]},{id:`method-straight-line-controller-is-complete`,name:`is_complete`,signature:`is_complete() -> bool`,summary:`Report whether the distance is within the position tolerance.`,returns:{type:`bool`,description:`Completion state.`}}]}]},{id:`data-types`,title:`Data types`,introduction:`These read-only records store sensor readings, motion requests, controller outputs, pose, and planning data passed between UCSBXRP classes. Construct a record by calling its class with the named inputs below, then read its fields by name. These are validated, read-only values; a tuple position is not part of the interface.`,entries:[{id:`record-reflectance-readings`,name:`ReflectanceReadings`,symbols:[`ReflectanceReadings`],kind:`value record`,purpose:`Contains the left and right floor-sensor readings, normalized from 0 for light to 1 for dark.`,signature:`ReflectanceReadings(left, right)`,properties:[{name:`left`,type:`float`,description:`Left reflectance, from 0 for a light floor to 1 for a dark line.`},{name:`right`,type:`float`,description:`Right reflectance, from 0 for a light floor to 1 for a dark line.`}],exceptions:[`TypeError if either reading is Boolean or nonnumeric.`,`ValueError if either reading is nonfinite or outside [0, 1].`]},{id:`record-raw-sensors`,name:`RawSensors`,symbols:[`RawSensors`],kind:`value record`,purpose:`Contains one hardware sample: encoder counts, timestamp, button state, and available range or floor-sensor readings.`,signature:`RawSensors(time_ms, left_encoder_count, right_encoder_count, range_mm, button_pressed, reflectance=None)`,properties:[{name:`time_ms`,type:`int`,units:`ms`,description:`Device timestamp.`},{name:`left_encoder_count`,type:`int`,units:`count`,description:`Left encoder count relative to the latest reset.`},{name:`right_encoder_count`,type:`int`,units:`count`,description:`Right encoder count relative to the latest reset.`},{name:`range_mm`,type:`float | None`,units:`mm`,description:`Ultrasonic range, or None when unavailable or not requested.`},{name:`button_pressed`,type:`bool`,description:`Current USER-button state.`},{name:`reflectance`,type:`ReflectanceReadings | None`,description:`Floor readings, or None when unavailable or not requested.`}],exceptions:[`TypeError if time_ms or an encoder count is not an integer, button_pressed is not Boolean, or range_mm is Boolean or nonnumeric.`,`ValueError if time_ms is negative or range_mm is nonfinite or not greater than zero.`]},{id:`record-measurements`,name:`Measurements`,symbols:[`Measurements`],kind:`value record`,purpose:`Contains wheel travel, increments, speed estimates, elapsed sample time, and available range and floor-sensor readings. SensorModel creates this record from RawSensors.`,signature:`Measurements(time_ms, dt_s, left_position_mm, right_position_mm, left_increment_mm, right_increment_mm, left_speed_mm_s, right_speed_mm_s, range_mm, button_pressed, reflectance=None)`,properties:[{name:`time_ms`,type:`int`,units:`ms`,description:`Device timestamp.`},{name:`dt_s`,type:`float`,units:`s`,description:`Elapsed time from the preceding sample.`},{name:`left_position_mm`,type:`float`,units:`mm`,description:`Cumulative left-wheel travel since reset.`},{name:`right_position_mm`,type:`float`,units:`mm`,description:`Cumulative right-wheel travel since reset.`},{name:`left_increment_mm`,type:`float`,units:`mm`,description:`Unsmoothed left-wheel travel since the preceding sample.`},{name:`right_increment_mm`,type:`float`,units:`mm`,description:`Unsmoothed right-wheel travel since the preceding sample.`},{name:`left_speed_mm_s`,type:`float`,units:`mm/s`,description:`Left-wheel speed estimate formed from recent encoder samples.`},{name:`right_speed_mm_s`,type:`float`,units:`mm/s`,description:`Right-wheel speed estimate formed from recent encoder samples.`},{name:`range_mm`,type:`float | None`,units:`mm`,description:`Range reading or None.`},{name:`button_pressed`,type:`bool`,description:`USER-button state.`},{name:`reflectance`,type:`ReflectanceReadings | None`,description:`Preserved floor readings, or None.`},{name:`wheel_speeds`,type:`WheelSpeeds`,description:`Left and right speed estimates as one value.`}],exceptions:[`TypeError if a numeric argument is Boolean or nonnumeric, time_ms is not an integer, or button_pressed is not Boolean.`,`ValueError if time_ms or dt_s is negative, a number is nonfinite, or a supplied range is not greater than zero.`]},{id:`record-wheel-speeds`,name:`WheelSpeeds`,symbols:[`WheelSpeeds`],kind:`value record`,purpose:`Contains two wheel speeds, accessed as left_mm_s and right_mm_s. The same record type represents requested or measured speeds; the variable holding it identifies which.`,signature:`WheelSpeeds(left_mm_s, right_mm_s)`,properties:[{name:`left_mm_s`,type:`float`,units:`mm/s`,description:`Left-wheel speed.`},{name:`right_mm_s`,type:`float`,units:`mm/s`,description:`Right-wheel speed.`}],exceptions:[`TypeError if either wheel speed is Boolean or nonnumeric.`,`ValueError if either wheel speed is not finite.`],constructorExample:`speeds = WheelSpeeds(left_mm_s=89.0, right_mm_s=151.0)
print(speeds.left_mm_s, speeds.right_mm_s)`},{id:`record-motion-command`,name:`MotionCommand`,symbols:[`MotionCommand`],kind:`value record`,purpose:`Contains the requested forward speed and counterclockwise turn rate, accessed as forward_speed_mm_s and turn_rate_rad_s. Constructing this record stores the request; Robot.step(command) applies it.`,signature:`MotionCommand(forward_speed_mm_s, turn_rate_rad_s)`,properties:[{name:`forward_speed_mm_s`,type:`float`,units:`mm/s`,description:`Requested forward speed.`},{name:`turn_rate_rad_s`,type:`float`,units:`rad/s`,description:`Requested counterclockwise turn rate.`}],exceptions:[`TypeError if either argument is Boolean or nonnumeric.`,`ValueError if either argument is not finite.`],constructorExample:`command = MotionCommand(forward_speed_mm_s=120.0, turn_rate_rad_s=0.4)
print(command.forward_speed_mm_s, command.turn_rate_rad_s)`},{id:`record-drive-command`,name:`DriveCommand`,symbols:[`DriveCommand`,`MotorEfforts`],kind:`value record`,purpose:`Contains normalized left and right motor commands in the range -1 to 1. Positive values request forward wheel motion; hardware wiring signs are applied when the command is sent.`,signature:`DriveCommand(left, right)`,properties:[{name:`left`,type:`float`,description:`Left command in [-1.0, 1.0].`},{name:`right`,type:`float`,description:`Right command in [-1.0, 1.0].`}],exceptions:[`TypeError if either command is Boolean or nonnumeric.`,`ValueError if either command is nonfinite or outside [-1.0, 1.0].`],notes:[`MotorEfforts is a compatibility name for the same type. Use DriveCommand in new code.`]},{id:`record-pose`,name:`Pose`,symbols:[`Pose`],kind:`value record`,purpose:`Contains x position, y position, and heading in world coordinates. Heading zero points along +x; positive heading turns counterclockwise toward +y.`,signature:`Pose(x_mm, y_mm, heading_rad)`,properties:[{name:`x_mm`,type:`float`,units:`mm`,description:`World x position.`},{name:`y_mm`,type:`float`,units:`mm`,description:`World y position.`},{name:`heading_rad`,type:`float`,units:`rad`,description:`Heading wrapped to [-pi, pi).`}],exceptions:[`TypeError if a coordinate or heading is Boolean or nonnumeric.`,`ValueError if a coordinate or heading is not finite.`]},{id:`record-robot-state`,name:`RobotState`,symbols:[`RobotState`],kind:`value record`,purpose:`Contains the measurements and estimated pose returned by Robot.start() or Robot.step(). Read them as state.measurements and state.pose.`,signature:`RobotState(measurements: Measurements, pose: Pose)`,properties:[{name:`measurements`,type:`Measurements`,description:`Sensor-derived values.`},{name:`pose`,type:`Pose`,description:`Odometry estimate.`}],exceptions:[`TypeError if measurements is not Measurements or pose is not Pose.`]},{id:`record-navigation-goal`,name:`NavigationGoal`,symbols:[`NavigationGoal`],kind:`value record`,purpose:`Contains a destination x and y position and an optional heading to reach there.`,signature:`NavigationGoal(x_mm, y_mm, heading_rad=None)`,properties:[{name:`x_mm`,type:`float`,units:`mm`,description:`Destination x position.`},{name:`y_mm`,type:`float`,units:`mm`,description:`Destination y position.`},{name:`heading_rad`,type:`float | None`,units:`rad`,description:`Required final heading, or None for position only.`}],exceptions:[`TypeError if a coordinate or supplied heading is Boolean or nonnumeric.`,`ValueError if a coordinate or supplied heading is not finite.`]},{id:`record-grid-cell`,name:`GridCell`,symbols:[`GridCell`],kind:`value record`,purpose:`Contains integer column and row indices identifying one occupancy-grid cell.`,signature:`GridCell(column, row)`,properties:[{name:`column`,type:`int`,description:`Column increasing with world x.`},{name:`row`,type:`int`,description:`Row increasing with world y.`}],exceptions:[`TypeError if column or row is not an integer.`]},{id:`record-grid-path`,name:`GridPath`,symbols:[`GridPath`],kind:`value record`,purpose:`Contains an ordered route of grid cells. Consecutive cells share an edge.`,signature:`GridPath(cells)`,properties:[{name:`cells`,type:`tuple[GridCell, ...]`,description:`Nonempty route of horizontally or vertically adjacent cells.`}],exceptions:[`TypeError if cells is not a tuple or list or contains a value other than GridCell.`,`ValueError if cells is empty or consecutive cells do not share a horizontal or vertical edge.`],methods:[{id:`method-grid-path-to-goals`,name:`to_goals`,signature:`to_goals(grid: OccupancyGrid, final_heading_rad: float | None = None) -> tuple[NavigationGoal, ...]`,summary:`Convert the route to compact goals at turns and the final cell.`,parameters:[{name:`grid`,type:`OccupancyGrid`,description:`Grid used to convert cell centers to world coordinates.`},{name:`final_heading_rad`,type:`float | None`,default:`None`,units:`rad`,description:`Optional heading required at the final goal.`}],returns:{type:`tuple[NavigationGoal, ...]`,description:`World-coordinate navigation goals.`},exceptions:[`AttributeError if grid does not provide cell_center().`,`TypeError if final_heading_rad is Boolean or nonnumeric, or grid.cell_center() rejects a path cell's type.`,`ValueError if final_heading_rad is not finite or grid.cell_center() rejects a cell outside the grid.`]}]},{id:`constant-stop-command`,name:`STOP_COMMAND`,symbols:[`STOP_COMMAND`],kind:`constant`,purpose:`Shared zero-motion request.`,signature:`STOP_COMMAND = MotionCommand(0.0, 0.0)`}]},{id:`configuration`,title:`Configuration`,introduction:`Robot settings belong in robot_config.py. Each configuration object is read-only after construction.`,entries:[{id:`class-robot-config`,name:`RobotConfig`,symbols:[`RobotConfig`],kind:`configuration record`,purpose:`Contains robot geometry, sensor sampling settings, motor calibration, and wheel-speed feedback settings. The component methods read the relevant values from self.config.`,signature:`RobotConfig()`,properties:[{name:`sample_period_ms`,type:`int`,default:`20`,units:`ms`,description:`Scheduled interval between Robot samples; integer at least 1.`},{name:`wheel_diameter_mm`,type:`float`,default:`60.0`,units:`mm`,description:`Measured wheel diameter used to convert encoder revolutions to wheel travel; greater than zero.`},{name:`encoder_counts_per_revolution`,type:`float`,default:`585.0`,units:`count/rev`,description:`Encoder counts corresponding to one wheel revolution; greater than zero.`},{name:`track_width_mm`,type:`float`,default:`155.0`,units:`mm`,description:`Effective lateral distance between the left and right wheel paths, used by DifferentialDrive and Odometry; greater than zero.`},{name:`left_motor_sign`,type:`int`,default:`1`,description:`+1 or -1, chosen so a positive left DriveCommand turns the left wheel forward.`},{name:`right_motor_sign`,type:`int`,default:`1`,description:`+1 or -1, chosen so a positive right DriveCommand turns the right wheel forward.`},{name:`left_encoder_sign`,type:`int`,default:`1`,description:`+1 or -1, chosen so forward left-wheel travel produces a positive count change.`},{name:`right_encoder_sign`,type:`int`,default:`1`,description:`+1 or -1, chosen so forward right-wheel travel produces a positive count change.`},{name:`left_start_command`,type:`float`,default:`0.0`,description:`Nonnegative left-wheel command needed to overcome motor deadband when a nonzero speed is requested.`},{name:`right_start_command`,type:`float`,default:`0.0`,description:`Nonnegative right-wheel command needed to overcome motor deadband when a nonzero speed is requested.`},{name:`left_speed_command_gain`,type:`float`,default:`0.0`,units:`s/mm`,description:`Left-wheel feedforward command per unit of requested wheel speed.`},{name:`right_speed_command_gain`,type:`float`,default:`0.0`,units:`s/mm`,description:`Right-wheel feedforward command per unit of requested wheel speed.`},{name:`wheel_speed_filter_time_constant_ms`,type:`float`,default:`80.0`,units:`ms`,description:`Additional response time of the wheel-speed estimate formed from recent encoder samples; zero selects the estimator's minimum supported response.`},{name:`wheel_speed_kp`,type:`float`,default:`0.0`,units:`s/mm`,description:`Proportional change in motor command per unit of wheel-speed error.`},{name:`max_drive_command`,type:`float`,default:`1.0`,description:`Maximum absolute DriveCommand sent to either motor; from 0.0 to 1.0 inclusive.`}],exceptions:[`TypeError if an argument has the wrong type, an unknown argument is supplied, or a current and older compatibility name are both supplied.`,`ValueError if a number is not finite or violates the range stated above, or if a starting command exceeds max_drive_command.`],notes:[`Every listed setting is optional in the constructor. Pass a named setting to replace its effective default; the table states those defaults. The example is illustrative, not measured calibration.`,`The listed values are effective constructor defaults. Course projects normally import measured ROBOT_CONFIG from robot_config.py; a default RobotConfig() is not calibrated for a particular physical XRP.`,`For compatibility with projects created before API 0.3, the implementation also accepts the older argument names ending in _effort. New projects should use the names above.`],constructorExample:`config = RobotConfig(
    sample_period_ms=20,
    wheel_speed_kp=0.001,
    max_drive_command=0.55,
)  # Illustrative settings; measure your own robot.`},{id:`class-navigation-config`,name:`NavigationConfig`,symbols:[`NavigationConfig`],kind:`configuration record`,purpose:`Contains travel speeds, turn rate, slowing distance, and the position and heading tolerances used by navigation.`,signature:`NavigationConfig(cruise_speed_mm_s, approach_speed_mm_s, slowdown_distance_mm, turn_rate_rad_s, position_tolerance_mm, heading_tolerance_rad, realign_heading_rad)`,properties:[{name:`cruise_speed_mm_s`,type:`float`,units:`mm/s`,description:`Normal forward speed away from a goal; greater than zero.`},{name:`approach_speed_mm_s`,type:`float`,units:`mm/s`,description:`Reduced forward speed near a goal; greater than zero and no greater than cruise_speed_mm_s.`},{name:`slowdown_distance_mm`,type:`float`,units:`mm`,description:`Remaining distance at which the controller changes from cruise speed to approach speed; greater than zero.`},{name:`turn_rate_rad_s`,type:`float`,units:`rad/s`,description:`Magnitude of the requested angular velocity while turning; greater than zero.`},{name:`position_tolerance_mm`,type:`float`,units:`mm`,description:`Maximum remaining planar distance accepted as reaching a goal; nonnegative.`},{name:`heading_tolerance_rad`,type:`float`,units:`rad`,description:`Maximum absolute heading error accepted as aligned; nonnegative.`},{name:`realign_heading_rad`,type:`float`,units:`rad`,description:`Absolute heading error at which forward travel stops for realignment; no smaller than heading_tolerance_rad.`}],exceptions:[`TypeError if an argument is Boolean or nonnumeric.`,`ValueError if a number is not finite or violates the range stated above, approach_speed_mm_s exceeds cruise_speed_mm_s, or realign_heading_rad is below heading_tolerance_rad.`],constructorExample:`navigation = NavigationConfig(
    cruise_speed_mm_s=150.0, approach_speed_mm_s=120.0,
    slowdown_distance_mm=120.0, turn_rate_rad_s=0.8,
    position_tolerance_mm=12.0, heading_tolerance_rad=0.08,
    realign_heading_rad=0.25,
)  # Illustrative project settings.`}]},{id:`live`,title:`Live controls and telemetry values`,introduction:`Import ucsb_xrp.live to create compact controls and publish selected program values to the Monitor. Declare controls once, then read each LiveParameter.value during the robot loop. Robot applies all pending control changes together after each Robot.start() or Robot.step() call.`,entries:[{id:`module-live`,name:`ucsb_xrp.live`,symbols:[`live`],kind:`module`,purpose:`Create Monitor controls and publish selected program values.`,state:`Retain declared controls and the latest watch and plot values for the current run. Robot applies all pending control changes together after each Robot.start() or Robot.step() call.`},{id:`class-live-parameter`,name:`LiveParameter`,symbols:[`LiveParameter`],kind:`value object`,purpose:`Represent one Monitor control and the value currently applied to the program.`,state:`The value changes only when live.apply_updates(), Robot.start(), or Robot.step() applies a pending Monitor setting.`,properties:[{name:`value`,type:`float | bool | str`,description:`Value currently applied to the program; read it but do not assign to it.`},{name:`name`,type:`str`,description:`Python-style identifier.`},{name:`label`,type:`str`,description:`Short Monitor label.`},{name:`kind`,type:`str`,description:`number, toggle, or choice.`},{name:`unit`,type:`str`,description:`Displayed unit or empty string.`},{name:`minimum`,type:`float | None`,description:`Numeric slider lower bound.`},{name:`maximum`,type:`float | None`,description:`Numeric slider upper bound.`},{name:`step`,type:`float | None`,description:`Numeric slider increment.`},{name:`options`,type:`tuple[str, ...]`,description:`Choice values, or an empty tuple.`}]},{id:`function-live-number`,name:`live.number`,symbols:[`number`],kind:`function`,purpose:`Declare a numeric slider with a minimum, maximum, and step size.`,signature:`live.number(name, default, minimum, maximum, step, unit='', label=None) -> LiveParameter`,parameters:[{name:`name`,type:`str`,description:`Unique Python-style identifier, at most 32 characters.`},{name:`default`,type:`float`,description:`Initial applied value.`},{name:`minimum`,type:`float`,description:`Inclusive lower bound.`},{name:`maximum`,type:`float`,description:`Inclusive upper bound.`},{name:`step`,type:`float`,description:`Positive slider increment.`},{name:`unit`,type:`str`,default:`''`,description:`Short displayed unit.`},{name:`label`,type:`str | None`,default:`None`,description:`Displayed label; derived from name when omitted.`}],returns:{type:`LiveParameter`,description:`Numeric control.`},requiredBehavior:[`maximum must exceed minimum; step must be positive and no larger than the range; default must lie inside the inclusive bounds.`,`The range does not need to contain an exact whole number of steps. The applied value is the nearest available step within the bounds.`],exceptions:[`TypeError if name, unit, or label is not a string or a numeric argument is Boolean or nonnumeric.`,`ValueError if text is empty or too long, name is not a Python identifier, a number is nonfinite, bounds or step are invalid, default lies outside the bounds, the name is already in use, or 16 controls already exist.`]},{id:`function-live-toggle`,name:`live.toggle`,symbols:[`toggle`],kind:`function`,purpose:`Declare an on/off control.`,signature:`live.toggle(name, default, label=None) -> LiveParameter`,parameters:[{name:`name`,type:`str`,description:`Unique Python-style identifier.`},{name:`default`,type:`bool`,description:`Initial applied state.`},{name:`label`,type:`str | None`,default:`None`,description:`Displayed label; derived from name when omitted.`}],returns:{type:`LiveParameter`,description:`Boolean control.`},exceptions:[`TypeError if name or label is not a string or default is not Boolean.`,`ValueError if text is empty or too long, name is not a Python identifier, the name is already in use, or 16 controls already exist.`]},{id:`function-live-choice`,name:`live.choice`,symbols:[`choice`],kind:`function`,purpose:`Declare a control with two to six string choices.`,signature:`live.choice(name, default, options, label=None) -> LiveParameter`,parameters:[{name:`name`,type:`str`,description:`Unique Python-style identifier.`},{name:`default`,type:`str`,description:`Initial applied choice; it must appear in options.`},{name:`options`,type:`sequence[str]`,description:`Two to six unique choices.`},{name:`label`,type:`str | None`,default:`None`,description:`Displayed label; derived from name when omitted.`}],returns:{type:`LiveParameter`,description:`Choice control.`},exceptions:[`TypeError if name, label, or any choice is not a string.`,`ValueError if text is empty or too long, name is not a Python identifier, options does not contain two to six unique choices, default is not one of them, the name is already in use, or 16 controls already exist.`]},{id:`function-live-watch`,name:`live.watch`,symbols:[`watch`],kind:`function`,purpose:`Publish the latest number, Boolean, or short string as a named live value.`,signature:`live.watch(name, value, unit='', label=None) -> None`,parameters:[{name:`name`,type:`str`,description:`Unique Python-style identifier.`},{name:`value`,type:`float | bool | str`,description:`Finite number, Boolean, or string of at most 64 characters.`},{name:`unit`,type:`str`,default:`''`,description:`Short displayed unit.`},{name:`label`,type:`str | None`,default:`None`,description:`Displayed label; derived from name when omitted.`}],returns:{type:`None`,description:`No value.`},exceptions:[`TypeError if name, unit, or label is not a string or value is not a number, Boolean, or string.`,`ValueError if text is empty or too long, name is not a Python identifier, a numeric value is nonfinite, or 16 watch values already exist.`]},{id:`function-live-plot`,name:`live.plot`,symbols:[`plot`],kind:`function`,purpose:`Publish a finite numeric value as an optional Monitor strip-plot signal.`,signature:`live.plot(name, value, unit='', label=None) -> None`,parameters:[{name:`name`,type:`str`,description:`Unique Python-style identifier.`},{name:`value`,type:`float`,description:`Finite numeric value for the current sample.`},{name:`unit`,type:`str`,default:`''`,description:`Short displayed unit.`},{name:`label`,type:`str | None`,default:`None`,description:`Displayed label; derived from name when omitted.`}],returns:{type:`None`,description:`No value.`},exceptions:[`TypeError if name, unit, or label is not a string or value is Boolean or nonnumeric.`,`ValueError if text is empty or too long, name is not a Python identifier, value is nonfinite, or 16 plot values already exist.`]},{id:`function-live-apply-updates`,name:`live.apply_updates`,symbols:[`apply_updates`],kind:`function`,purpose:`Apply all pending Monitor control changes together and report whether any applied value changed.`,signature:`live.apply_updates() -> bool`,returns:{type:`bool`,description:`True if at least one applied value changed.`},notes:[`Robot.start() and Robot.step() call this automatically. Call it directly only in a program that does not use Robot.`]}]},{id:`worlds-maps-missions`,title:`Worlds, maps, routes, and missions`,entries:[{id:`class-project-world`,name:`ProjectWorld`,symbols:[`ProjectWorld`],kind:`supplied class`,purpose:`Provide one named world loaded from the project's world.json file, including bounds, initial pose, fixed obstacles, changeable features, and waypoint markers.`,state:`The loaded world does not change. arena_map() creates a new ArenaMap, and waypoint methods create NavigationGoal values from the stored markers.`,properties:[{name:`id`,type:`str`,description:`World identifier.`},{name:`label`,type:`str`,description:`Display name.`},{name:`bounds_mm`,type:`tuple[float, float, float, float]`,units:`mm`,description:`World bounds.`},{name:`initial_pose`,type:`Pose`,description:`Configured start pose.`},{name:`feature_names`,type:`tuple[str, ...]`,description:`Named changeable obstacle features.`}],methods:[{id:`method-project-world-arena-map`,name:`arena_map`,signature:`arena_map(blocked_features=()) -> ArenaMap`,summary:`Build an arena map with selected features blocked.`,parameters:[{name:`blocked_features`,type:`sequence[str]`,default:`()`,description:`Feature names that should act as obstacles.`}],returns:{type:`ArenaMap`,description:`Arena geometry with the named features marked as obstacles.`},exceptions:[`ValueError if blocked_features contains a name not present in feature_names.`]},{id:`method-project-world-waypoint`,name:`waypoint`,signature:`waypoint(name: str) -> NavigationGoal`,summary:`Return one named waypoint.`,parameters:[{name:`name`,type:`str`,description:`Waypoint name from world.json.`}],returns:{type:`NavigationGoal`,description:`Waypoint goal.`},exceptions:[`ValueError if no waypoint has that name or its stored coordinates are invalid.`]},{id:`method-project-world-waypoints`,name:`waypoints`,signature:`waypoints() -> tuple[NavigationGoal, ...]`,summary:`Return all waypoints in file order.`,returns:{type:`tuple[NavigationGoal, ...]`,description:`Waypoint sequence.`}}]},{id:`function-load-world`,name:`load_world`,symbols:[`load_world`],kind:`function`,purpose:`Load the default or named world from a project JSON file.`,signature:`load_world(path='world.json', world_id=None) -> ProjectWorld`,parameters:[{name:`path`,type:`str`,default:`'world.json'`,description:`Project world file.`},{name:`world_id`,type:`str | None`,default:`None`,description:`World identifier; None selects default_world.`}],returns:{type:`ProjectWorld`,description:`Selected ProjectWorld loaded from world.json.`},exceptions:[`OSError if path cannot be opened.`,`ValueError if the JSON, world list, selected world, bounds, coordinates, or names are invalid.`,`TypeError if a world field has the wrong JSON type.`]},{id:`class-rectangle`,name:`Rectangle`,symbols:[`Rectangle`],kind:`value record`,purpose:`Represent a closed axis-aligned rectangle in world millimeters.`,signature:`Rectangle(minimum_x_mm, minimum_y_mm, maximum_x_mm, maximum_y_mm)`,properties:[{name:`minimum_x_mm`,type:`float`,units:`mm`,description:`Minimum x boundary.`},{name:`minimum_y_mm`,type:`float`,units:`mm`,description:`Minimum y boundary.`},{name:`maximum_x_mm`,type:`float`,units:`mm`,description:`Maximum x boundary; greater than minimum_x_mm.`},{name:`maximum_y_mm`,type:`float`,units:`mm`,description:`Maximum y boundary; greater than minimum_y_mm.`},{name:`bounds_mm`,type:`tuple[float, float, float, float]`,units:`mm`,description:`Minimum and maximum x and y bounds.`}],exceptions:[`TypeError if a boundary is Boolean or nonnumeric.`,`ValueError if a boundary is nonfinite or the rectangle does not have positive width and height.`],methods:[{id:`method-rectangle-contains`,name:`contains`,signature:`contains(x_mm, y_mm, margin_mm=0.0) -> bool`,summary:`Test whether a point lies inside bounds expanded by margin_mm.`,parameters:[{name:`x_mm`,type:`float`,units:`mm`,description:`Point x coordinate.`},{name:`y_mm`,type:`float`,units:`mm`,description:`Point y coordinate.`},{name:`margin_mm`,type:`float`,default:`0.0`,units:`mm`,description:`Nonnegative outward expansion.`}],returns:{type:`bool`,description:`Containment result.`},exceptions:[`TypeError if a coordinate or margin is Boolean or nonnumeric.`,`ValueError if a coordinate is nonfinite or margin_mm is nonfinite or negative.`]}]},{id:`class-arena-map`,name:`ArenaMap`,symbols:[`ArenaMap`],kind:`supplied class`,purpose:`Represent rectangular arena bounds, fixed obstacles, and named changeable obstacle features.`,state:`The map does not change after construction. with_feature_blocked() returns a new ArenaMap rather than modifying the current map.`,signature:`ArenaMap(bounds_mm, obstacles=(), features=None, blocked_features=())`,parameters:[{name:`bounds_mm`,type:`Rectangle | sequence[float]`,units:`mm`,description:`Arena bounds as a Rectangle or four-number bounds.`},{name:`obstacles`,type:`sequence[Rectangle]`,default:`()`,description:`Fixed obstacles.`},{name:`features`,type:`dict[str, Rectangle] | None`,default:`None`,description:`Named changeable rectangles.`},{name:`blocked_features`,type:`sequence[str]`,default:`()`,description:`Feature names initially treated as obstacles.`}],exceptions:[`TypeError if bounds or obstacles are not rectangles or four-number bounds, obstacles is not a sequence, features is not a dictionary of named rectangles, or a feature name is empty or nontext.`,`ValueError if a rectangle is invalid or blocked_features contains an unknown name.`],properties:[{name:`bounds_mm`,type:`tuple[float, float, float, float]`,units:`mm`,description:`Arena bounds.`},{name:`obstacles`,type:`tuple[Rectangle, ...]`,description:`Fixed obstacles.`},{name:`feature_names`,type:`tuple[str, ...]`,description:`Named features.`},{name:`blocked_features`,type:`tuple[str, ...]`,description:`Features currently treated as obstacles.`}],methods:[{id:`method-arena-map-feature-bounds`,name:`feature_bounds`,signature:`feature_bounds(name: str) -> tuple[float, float, float, float]`,summary:`Return one feature's bounds.`,parameters:[{name:`name`,type:`str`,description:`Known feature name.`}],returns:{type:`tuple[float, float, float, float]`,description:`Feature bounds in millimeters.`},exceptions:[`ValueError if name is not a known feature.`]},{id:`method-arena-map-contains`,name:`contains`,signature:`contains(x_mm, y_mm) -> bool`,summary:`Test whether a point lies inside the arena.`,parameters:[{name:`x_mm`,type:`float`,units:`mm`,description:`Point x coordinate.`},{name:`y_mm`,type:`float`,units:`mm`,description:`Point y coordinate.`}],returns:{type:`bool`,description:`True inside or on the arena boundary.`},exceptions:[`TypeError if a coordinate is Boolean or nonnumeric.`,`ValueError if a coordinate is not finite.`]},{id:`method-arena-map-is-free`,name:`is_free`,signature:`is_free(x_mm, y_mm, clearance_mm=0.0) -> bool`,summary:`Test arena and obstacle clearance.`,parameters:[{name:`x_mm`,type:`float`,units:`mm`,description:`Point x coordinate.`},{name:`y_mm`,type:`float`,units:`mm`,description:`Point y coordinate.`},{name:`clearance_mm`,type:`float`,default:`0.0`,units:`mm`,description:`Required nonnegative distance from walls and obstacles.`}],returns:{type:`bool`,description:`True when the point satisfies the requested clearance.`},exceptions:[`TypeError if a coordinate or clearance is Boolean or nonnumeric.`,`ValueError if a coordinate is nonfinite or clearance_mm is nonfinite or negative.`]},{id:`method-arena-map-with-feature-blocked`,name:`with_feature_blocked`,signature:`with_feature_blocked(name: str, blocked: bool) -> ArenaMap`,summary:`Return a new map with one feature's blocked state changed.`,parameters:[{name:`name`,type:`str`,description:`Known feature name.`},{name:`blocked`,type:`bool`,description:`Whether the feature should act as an obstacle.`}],returns:{type:`ArenaMap`,description:`New immutable map.`},exceptions:[`ValueError if name is not a known feature.`,`TypeError if blocked is not Boolean.`]}]},{id:`class-occupancy-grid`,name:`OccupancyGrid`,symbols:[`OccupancyGrid`],kind:`supplied class`,purpose:`Sample an ArenaMap into uniform free and blocked cells.`,state:`Grid resolution, origin, dimensions, and blocked cells do not change after from_arena() creates the grid.`,signature:`OccupancyGrid.from_arena(arena: ArenaMap, resolution_mm: float, clearance_mm: float = 0.0) -> OccupancyGrid`,parameters:[{name:`arena`,type:`ArenaMap`,description:`Arena geometry to sample.`},{name:`resolution_mm`,type:`float`,units:`mm`,description:`Positive square-cell size.`},{name:`clearance_mm`,type:`float`,default:`0.0`,units:`mm`,description:`Nonnegative obstacle and wall clearance.`}],exceptions:[`TypeError if arena is not ArenaMap or a numeric argument is Boolean or nonnumeric.`,`ValueError if resolution_mm is nonfinite or not greater than zero, or clearance_mm is nonfinite or negative.`],properties:[{name:`resolution_mm`,type:`float`,units:`mm`,description:`Cell size.`},{name:`origin_x_mm`,type:`float`,units:`mm`,description:`Grid minimum x.`},{name:`origin_y_mm`,type:`float`,units:`mm`,description:`Grid minimum y.`},{name:`column_count`,type:`int`,description:`Number of columns.`},{name:`row_count`,type:`int`,description:`Number of rows.`}],methods:[{id:`method-occupancy-grid-world-to-cell`,name:`world_to_cell`,signature:`world_to_cell(x_mm, y_mm) -> GridCell | None`,summary:`Convert a world point to a cell or None outside the grid.`,parameters:[{name:`x_mm`,type:`float`,units:`mm`,description:`World x coordinate.`},{name:`y_mm`,type:`float`,units:`mm`,description:`World y coordinate.`}],returns:{type:`GridCell | None`,description:`Containing cell, or None outside the grid.`},exceptions:[`TypeError if a coordinate is Boolean or nonnumeric.`,`ValueError if a coordinate is not finite.`]},{id:`method-occupancy-grid-cell-center`,name:`cell_center`,signature:`cell_center(cell: GridCell) -> tuple[float, float]`,summary:`Return a cell center in world millimeters.`,parameters:[{name:`cell`,type:`GridCell`,description:`Cell inside the grid.`}],returns:{type:`tuple[float, float]`,description:`World x and y coordinates in millimeters.`},exceptions:[`TypeError if cell is not GridCell.`,`ValueError if cell lies outside the grid.`]},{id:`method-occupancy-grid-contains`,name:`contains`,signature:`contains(cell: GridCell) -> bool`,summary:`Test whether a cell is inside the grid.`,parameters:[{name:`cell`,type:`GridCell`,description:`Cell to test.`}],returns:{type:`bool`,description:`True when row and column are in bounds.`},exceptions:[`TypeError if cell is not GridCell.`]},{id:`method-occupancy-grid-is-blocked`,name:`is_blocked`,signature:`is_blocked(cell: GridCell) -> bool`,summary:`Report blocked state; cells outside the grid are blocked.`,parameters:[{name:`cell`,type:`GridCell`,description:`Cell to test.`}],returns:{type:`bool`,description:`Blocked state.`},exceptions:[`TypeError if cell is not GridCell.`]},{id:`method-occupancy-grid-neighbors`,name:`neighbors`,signature:`neighbors(cell: GridCell) -> tuple[GridCell, ...]`,summary:`Return free cells sharing a horizontal or vertical edge.`,parameters:[{name:`cell`,type:`GridCell`,description:`Reference cell.`}],returns:{type:`tuple[GridCell, ...]`,description:`Free edge-adjacent cells in deterministic order.`},exceptions:[`TypeError if cell is not GridCell.`]}],notes:[`For direct software tests, the full constructor accepts resolution_mm, origin_x_mm, origin_y_mm, column_count, row_count, and row-major blocked values. Course projects normally use from_arena().`],example:{title:`Example: sample an arena into grid cells`,code:`from ucsb_xrp import ArenaMap, OccupancyGrid, Rectangle

arena = ArenaMap(Rectangle(0.0, 0.0, 300.0, 200.0))
grid = OccupancyGrid.from_arena(arena, resolution_mm=100.0)`}},{id:`record-delivery-task`,name:`DeliveryTask`,symbols:[`DeliveryTask`],kind:`value record`,purpose:`Store the fixed values needed for one supplied delivery mission.`,signature:`DeliveryTask(initial_pose, arena, grid_resolution_mm, clearance_mm, destination, observed_feature_name, range_sample_count, minimum_usable_range_count, blocked_range_threshold_mm, assume_blocked_without_range)`,properties:[{name:`initial_pose`,type:`Pose`,description:`Robot pose at mission start.`},{name:`arena`,type:`ArenaMap`,description:`Arena before the observed feature is classified.`},{name:`grid_resolution_mm`,type:`float`,units:`mm`,description:`Positive occupancy-grid cell size.`},{name:`clearance_mm`,type:`float`,units:`mm`,description:`Nonnegative planning clearance.`},{name:`destination`,type:`NavigationGoal`,description:`Delivery destination and optional final heading.`},{name:`observed_feature_name`,type:`str`,description:`Arena feature classified by the range observation.`},{name:`range_sample_count`,type:`int`,description:`Positive number of range samples to collect.`},{name:`minimum_usable_range_count`,type:`int`,description:`Positive minimum usable readings, no greater than range_sample_count.`},{name:`blocked_range_threshold_mm`,type:`float`,units:`mm`,description:`Positive range at or below which the observed feature is treated as blocked.`},{name:`assume_blocked_without_range`,type:`bool`,description:`Blocked state used when no range estimate is available.`}],exceptions:[`TypeError if initial_pose, arena, destination, a numeric setting, or assume_blocked_without_range has the wrong type.`,`ValueError if observed_feature_name is unknown, a count is below one, minimum_usable_range_count exceeds range_sample_count, or a numeric setting is nonfinite or outside its stated range.`]},{id:`class-delivery-mission`,name:`DeliveryMission`,symbols:[`DeliveryMission`],kind:`supplied class`,purpose:`Support the archived Delivery Mission project: observe range, update one map feature, plan a route, and navigate for a DeliveryTask. The current Out-and-Back challenge uses its own mission_steps.py and mission_policy.py instead.`,state:`Retain the task, latest range estimate, gate classification, planned path, number of navigation steps, and result. result is None before run(); no_path means no route was found; invalid_path means the planner returned cells that failed the path checks; destination_not_reached means navigation stopped outside the configured destination tolerances; delivered means the final estimated position and heading are within those tolerances.`,signature:`DeliveryMission(task: DeliveryTask, navigation: NavigationController, planner: GridPlanner)`,parameters:[{name:`task`,type:`DeliveryTask`,description:`Mission settings.`},{name:`navigation`,type:`NavigationController`,description:`Selected navigation component.`},{name:`planner`,type:`GridPlanner`,description:`Selected grid-planning component.`}],exceptions:[`TypeError if task is not DeliveryTask or navigation and planner do not provide the required public methods.`],properties:[{name:`task`,type:`DeliveryTask`,description:`Mission definition.`},{name:`range_estimate_mm`,type:`float | None`,units:`mm`,description:`Latest combined stationary range observation. None means no usable estimate was available or run() has not yet reached the observation.`},{name:`feature_blocked`,type:`bool | None`,description:`Latest blocked/open classification for task.observed_feature_name, or None before classification.`},{name:`planned_path`,type:`GridPath | None`,description:`Latest route returned by the planner. None means no route was found or planning has not yet occurred.`},{name:`navigation_step_count`,type:`int`,description:`Number of Robot.step navigation cycles executed by the latest run(), excluding stationary observation samples.`},{name:`result`,type:`str | None`,description:`delivered, no_path, invalid_path, destination_not_reached, or None before completion.`}],methods:[{id:`method-delivery-mission-run`,name:`run`,signature:`run(robot: Robot) -> RobotState`,summary:`Run the supplied delivery sequence and always attempt robot.stop().`,parameters:[{name:`robot`,type:`Robot`,description:`Assembled robot service.`}],returns:{type:`RobotState`,description:`Last robot state.`},exceptions:[`Exceptions raised by Robot, SensorModel, GridPlanner, NavigationController, or map construction. DeliveryMission always attempts robot.stop() before returning or re-raising. The IDE Stop control is the operator interruption path for a moving run.`]}]}]},{id:`hardware-math`,title:`Advanced: low-level XRP access and numerical functions`,entries:[{id:`class-xrpbot`,name:`XRPBot`,symbols:[`XRPBot`],kind:`supplied class`,purpose:`Read the XRP's encoders, clock, ultrasonic sensor, and USER button, and send normalized DriveCommand values to its motors. Ordinary course programs use Robot; use XRPBot directly only for low-level experiments.`,state:`Retain the RobotConfig and the encoder counts chosen as zero by reset_encoders().`,signature:`XRPBot(config: RobotConfig)`,parameters:[{name:`config`,type:`RobotConfig`,description:`Motor signs, encoder signs, and final command limit.`}],exceptions:[`TypeError if config is not a RobotConfig value.`,`Hardware exception if XRP devices cannot be initialized or stopped.`],properties:[{name:`config`,type:`RobotConfig`,description:`Hardware configuration.`},{name:`range_sample_seq`,type:`int | None`,description:`Identity of the latest requested ultrasound attempt in this run. Missing echoes have identities too. Repeated requests during the 70 ms minimum acquisition interval retain the same identity; None means no attempt is available in this run.`},{name:`range_sample_age_s`,type:`float | None`,units:`s`,description:`Elapsed time since that attempt completed, including an attempt with no usable echo. None before the first available attempt.`}],methods:[{id:`method-xrpbot-read`,name:`read`,signature:`read(include_range: bool = False, include_reflectance: bool = False) -> RawSensors`,summary:`Read encoders, time, button state, and optional range and reflectance.`,parameters:[{name:`include_range`,type:`bool`,default:`False`,description:`Request forward range; returns the most recent outcome during the 70 ms ultrasound interval. Check range_sample_seq and range_sample_age_s when freshness matters.`},{name:`include_reflectance`,type:`bool`,default:`False`,description:`Read the left and right reflectance sensors on this sample.`}],returns:{type:`RawSensors`,description:`Direct hardware sample.`},exceptions:[`TypeError if either include flag is not Boolean.`,`Hardware or run-stop exception while reading the XRP.`]},{id:`method-xrpbot-reset-encoders`,name:`reset_encoders`,signature:`reset_encoders() -> None`,summary:`Use current hardware counts as the session zero.`,returns:{type:`None`,description:`No value.`},exceptions:[`Hardware or run-stop exception while reading encoder counts.`]},{id:`method-xrpbot-wait-for-button`,name:`wait_for_button`,signature:`wait_for_button() -> None`,summary:`Wait for the XRP USER button.`,returns:{type:`None`,description:`No value.`},exceptions:[`Hardware or run-stop exception while waiting.`]},{id:`method-xrpbot-set-drive`,name:`set_drive`,signature:`set_drive(command: DriveCommand) -> None`,summary:`Apply one normalized motor command after configured signs and limits.`,parameters:[{name:`command`,type:`DriveCommand`,description:`Logical left and right motor commands.`}],returns:{type:`None`,description:`No value.`},exceptions:[`TypeError if command is not DriveCommand.`,`ValueError if a command field is not a finite real number.`,`Hardware or run-stop exception while writing the motors; XRPBot attempts to stop both motors before re-raising.`]},{id:`method-xrpbot-stop`,name:`stop`,signature:`stop() -> None`,summary:`Attempt to stop both motors.`,returns:{type:`None`,description:`No value.`},exceptions:[`Hardware exception if either motor cannot be set to zero.`]}],notes:[`set_efforts() is a compatibility alias for set_drive().`]},{id:`function-clamp`,name:`clamp`,symbols:[`clamp`],kind:`function`,purpose:`Limit a numeric value to an inclusive interval.`,signature:`clamp(value, lower, upper) -> float`,parameters:[{name:`value`,type:`float`,description:`Value to limit.`},{name:`lower`,type:`float`,description:`Inclusive lower bound.`},{name:`upper`,type:`float`,description:`Inclusive upper bound; not less than lower.`}],returns:{type:`float`,description:`The input value limited to [lower, upper].`},exceptions:[`TypeError if an argument is Boolean or nonnumeric.`,`ValueError if an argument is not finite or lower exceeds upper.`]},{id:`function-elapsed-time-s`,name:`elapsed_time_s`,symbols:[`elapsed_time_s`],kind:`function`,purpose:`Calculate a MicroPython-tick-safe elapsed interval in seconds.`,signature:`elapsed_time_s(later_ms: int, earlier_ms: int) -> float`,parameters:[{name:`later_ms`,type:`int`,units:`ms`,description:`Later device timestamp.`},{name:`earlier_ms`,type:`int`,units:`ms`,description:`Earlier device timestamp.`}],returns:{type:`float`,description:`Wrap-safe elapsed time in seconds.`},exceptions:[`TypeError if either timestamp is Boolean or not an integer.`]},{id:`function-wrap-angle-rad`,name:`wrap_angle_rad`,symbols:[`wrap_angle_rad`],kind:`function`,purpose:`Return the equivalent angle in [-pi, pi).`,signature:`wrap_angle_rad(angle_rad: float) -> float`,parameters:[{name:`angle_rad`,type:`float`,units:`rad`,description:`Angle to wrap.`}],returns:{type:`float`,description:`Equivalent angle in [-pi, pi).`},exceptions:[`TypeError if angle_rad is Boolean or nonnumeric.`,`ValueError if angle_rad is not finite.`]},{id:`function-distance-to-goal`,name:`distance_to_goal`,symbols:[`distance_to_goal`],kind:`function`,purpose:`Calculate planar distance from a pose to a navigation goal in millimeters.`,signature:`distance_to_goal(pose: Pose, goal: NavigationGoal) -> float`,parameters:[{name:`pose`,type:`Pose`,description:`Current world pose.`},{name:`goal`,type:`NavigationGoal`,description:`Destination position.`}],returns:{type:`float`,description:`Euclidean position error in millimeters.`},exceptions:[`AttributeError if pose or goal does not provide x_mm and y_mm.`,`TypeError if a coordinate is Boolean or nonnumeric.`,`ValueError if a coordinate is not finite.`]},{id:`function-bearing-to-goal`,name:`bearing_to_goal`,symbols:[`bearing_to_goal`],kind:`function`,purpose:`Calculate wrapped world-frame bearing from a pose to a navigation goal.`,signature:`bearing_to_goal(pose: Pose, goal: NavigationGoal) -> float`,parameters:[{name:`pose`,type:`Pose`,description:`Current world pose.`},{name:`goal`,type:`NavigationGoal`,description:`Destination position.`}],returns:{type:`float`,description:`World-frame bearing in [-pi, pi) radians.`},exceptions:[`AttributeError if pose or goal does not provide x_mm and y_mm.`,`TypeError if a coordinate is Boolean or nonnumeric.`,`ValueError if a coordinate is not finite.`]}]}],startHere:[{title:`Implement the assigned class`,anchor:`components`,description:`Find the class named in README.md and keep its listed method signatures and return types.`},{title:`Run a robot program`,anchor:`robot`,description:`Use course_setup.make_robot(ROBOT_CONFIG), then start(), step(), and stop().`},{title:`Read the result of robot.step()`,anchor:`record-robot-state`,description:`RobotState gives the newest Measurements and Pose.`},{title:`Plan a grid route`,anchor:`grid-planner`,description:`Build an OccupancyGrid from an ArenaMap, then call GridPlanner.plan().`}]};export{e as t};